1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Your car alarm goes off

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
at two in the morning — again — and nothing's wrong.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
No broken glass, no forced entry.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Just the alarm, blaring, for no clear reason.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Most random alarms trace back to one of two things —

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
the hood latch switch, or the key fob battery.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A loose hood pin switch can send a false "break-in" signal.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
A weak fob battery can do the same thing.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Checking those two spots first

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
can rule out the most common causes before anything else.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
One clue, easy to check.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
